          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of strict 2-group is a strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} vertical categorification
            of that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %p
            A strict 2-group is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          %p
            This means that it is a groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            equipped with a product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdot : G \times G \to G
            that behaves like the product in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          %p
            More general
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            incarnation of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
          %p
            We may think of any 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            in terms of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            with a single object, with morphisms the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} 2-morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a strict 2-group, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is a strict 2-groupoid. This is often a useful point of view. In particular, the general strictification result of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategories
            implies that any such 2-groupoid is equivalent to a strict one. So, up to the right notion of equivalence, strict 2-groups already exhaust all 2-groups; we just have to take care to allow for
            %em homomorphisms
            of these
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-groups," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "s.)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-group"} Lie 2-group
          %p
            Strict 2-groups are also equivalently encoded in terms of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_2 \to G_1)
            of ordinary groups:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
            is the group of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            the group of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            whose source is the neutral element in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
          %p In applications it is usually useful to pass back and forth between the 2-groupoid incarnation of strict 2-groups and their incarnation as crossed modules. The first perspective makes transparent many constructions, while the second perspective gives a useful means to do computations with 2-groups. The translation between the two points of view is described in detail below.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            A
            %strong
              strict
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
            is equivalently:
          %ul
            %li
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            %li
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            %li
              an internal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %li
              an internal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            %li
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-groupoid"} strict 2-groupoid
              with one object.
          %h2#expanding_the_definition Expanding the definition
          %p We examine the first definition in more detail.
          %p Copying and adapting from the entry on general internal categories we have:
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            is
          %ul
            %li
              %p a collection of group homomorphisms of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ,
                          %mi t
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C_1 \stackrel{s,t}{\to} C_0 \stackrel{i}{\to} C_1
              %p
                such that the composites
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\cdot i
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\cdot i
                are the identity morphisms on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo ,
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1 \times_{t,s} C_1
                for the pullback,
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mrow
                                  %mi t
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi s
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mi t
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi s
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      C_1 \times_{t,s} C_1 &amp;\to&amp; C_1
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{t}
                      \\\
                      C_1 &amp;\stackrel{s}{\to}&amp; C_0
                      }
              %p there is, in addition, a homomorphism
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo ,
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi comp
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C_1 \times_{t,s} C_1 \stackrel{comp}{\to} C_1
              %p
                “respecting
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                and
                = succeed "\u201D;" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %li
              %p
                such that the
                %em composition
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi comp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp
                is associative and unital with respect to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                “in the obvious way”.
          %h3#in_terms_of_strict_2groupoids In terms of strict 2-groupoids
          %p
            Every strict 2-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            defines a strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            – called its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            – defined by the fact that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                has a single object
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G(\bullet,\bullet) = G
                is the 2-group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                itself, regarded as a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %li
              %p
                the horizontal composition in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                is given by the group product operation on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Conversely, every strict 2-groupoid with a single object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet
            defines a 2-group this way.
          %p
            Beware, however, as discussed in detail at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            %em identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            in a way that respects morphisms between these objects, one needs to think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
            equipped with its unique pointing
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*} \to \mathbf{B}G
          %h3#InTermsOfCrossedModules In terms of crossed modules
          %p
            We describe how a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi δ
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\mathbf{B}G] = (G_2 \stackrel{\delta}{\to} G_1)
          %p
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\alpha
                  \\,\colon\,
                  G_1
                  \\longrightarrow
                  Aut(G_2)
          %p
            encodes a strict one-object 2-groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            There are four isomorphic but different ways to construct
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbf{B}G]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is taken to correspond to the product in the groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
          %p
            In concrete computations it happens that not all of these choices directly yield the expected formulas in terms of classical group theory from a given diagrammatics involving
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group+cohomology"} nonabelian group cohomology
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
          %p
            We now define the one-object strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            from the crossed module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi δ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\delta : G_2 \to G_1)
            with action
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : G_1 \to Aut(G_2)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                has a single
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bullet
            %li
              %p
                The set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} 1-morphisms
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                is the group
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
              .maruku-equation
